    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0497" n="417" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg417"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vignaud to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1035.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                        cable<anchor n="a" xml:id="d381-f1"/> of the 24th ultimo, instructing the
                    embassy to ascertain whether the French Government would have any objection to
                    our consuls using temporarily their good offices in representation of the
                    interests of Cuba and of its citizens, and to notify the consuls if permission
                    is granted.</p>
                <p>The French Government having promptly acquiesced in our desire, I have notified
                    Consuls-General Gowdy and Skinner and asked them to advise the consuls in their
                    respective districts.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Vignaud.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
